      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1904, Barstow’s grape growers earned a Silver Medal at the World’s Fair, showcasing the town’s agricultural excellence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barstow%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1904 Pecos River Dam break devastated local fruit and vegetable crops, a setback that echoed through the community for years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barstow%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
